id: pm-swarm-atomic-close
title: Adopt an atomic SDK close with fenced metadata changes
description: "Pinned PmClient.update auto-routes terminal status plus field/unset changes into a metadata update followed by a separate native close. CloseCommandOptions has no atomic custom-field/unset patch. Swarm now admits and compares every native commit and advances its expected snapshot only from the exact SDK onWrite successor; a later refusal reports committed native steps rather than claiming rollback. This preserves privacy and peer state, but does not establish a single-commit or all-or-nothing crash contract for compound close. Adopt a public SDK atomic guarded close when available; do not rebuild lifecycle/history behavior or compensate over foreign edits."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[2]: concurrency,sdk-gap
created_at: "2026-10-26T21:32:19.770Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-26T22:01:31.005Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: One guarded native item commit for close plus fencing fields and cleanup; interleaving and crash injection at every native transition; no lost peer changes or duplicate history; retain typed partial-state remedies until the SDK capability is available.
parent: pm-swarm-y972
comments[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-26T22:01:31.001Z",codex-agent,"Native compound-close regression and partial-prefix peer-preservation test pass. Separate behavioral reversions of the committed-successor observer and partial-commit refusal each fail their regression once, exit 1; restored positives pass. This verifies guarded per-stage behavior and truthful receipts, not a single atomic close. The SDK gap remains open."
